### BPMN Process Execution Flow API Tests
### These requests test the execution flow visualization endpoints

### Get Complete Execution Flow for BPMN Visualization
### This endpoint returns all executed elements, flows, boundary events, and execution cycles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/process-execution/{{processId}}/flow
Accept: application/json

###

### Get Execution Statistics Summary
### This endpoint returns execution stats without full flow details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/process-execution/{{processId}}/stats
Accept: application/json

###

### Example: Get execution flow for a specific process ID
### Replace {{processId}} with an actual process ID from your database
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc/flow
# Accept: application/json

###

### Example: Get execution stats for a specific process ID
### Replace {{processId}} with an actual process ID from your database
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc/stats
# Accept: application/json

###

### Test with different process states
### 1. Running process - should show partial execution
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/{{runningProcessId}}/flow

### 2. Completed process - should show full execution path
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/{{completedProcessId}}/flow

### 3. Failed process - should show execution up to failure point
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/{{failedProcessId}}/flow

###

### Test boundary event visualization
### Process with error boundary events - should show triggered boundaries
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/{{errorBoundaryProcessId}}/flow

###

### Test execution cycle analysis
### Complex process with parallel flows - should show multiple execution cycles
# GET http://localhost:5000/api/process-execution/{{parallelProcessId}}/flow

###

### Variables for easy testing
### Replace these with actual values from your database
@{
    "baseUrl": "http://localhost:5000",
    "processId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "runningProcessId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "completedProcessId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "failedProcessId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "errorBoundaryProcessId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "parallelProcessId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

